<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109462" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπουράνιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, and in <i><span class="en">
			Arat.
			134
		</span></i>
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>under heaven, under the sky,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύτατον δέρκεσθαι ὑπουρανίων πετεηνῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.675
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴδωλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					616
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					56
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ὑ.</span>
			<i>heavenly</i> beings, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Piet.</u>
				58
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>as far as heaven covers,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγα κέν οἱ ὑπουράνιον κλέος εἴη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.212
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.264
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
